    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Extract the invoice data from this document text:\n\n{{ $json.text }}",
        "messages": {
          "messageValues": [
            {
              "message": "You are a precise invoice data extraction engine. You read the text of ONE business document and return a single JSON object, nothing else.\n\nRULES (follow strictly):\n1. Use ONLY information that is explicitly present in the text. NEVER guess, infer, calculate or invent a value. If a field is missing, unclear or ambiguous, set it to null.\n2. Copy numbers exactly as printed. Do NOT recompute subtotal, tax or total, and do NOT fix arithmetic errors you notice. Report what the document says.\n3. Numbers: plain numbers only (no currency symbols, no thousands separators). 1,234.50 -> 1234.50\n4. invoice_date: ISO format YYYY-MM-DD. If the date is ambiguous (for example 03/04/2026) or incomplete, set null.\n5. currency: 3-letter ISO code (GBP, USD, EUR...). Only set it if a symbol or code appears in the document, otherwise null.\n6. supplier_name is the company issuing the invoice (the seller). customer_name is the company being billed.\n7. line_items: every line in the document. Use null for any line value not shown. Do not add lines that are not there.\n8. The text may come from a spreadsheet (rows written as key: value) or from OCR; read it accordingly.\n9. confidence: for each of the 8 header fields give a number from 0 to 1 for how sure you are the value is correct (use 0 when the value is null).\n10. If the document is not an invoice, return all fields null, line_items [] and explain in notes.\n\nReturn exactly this JSON shape:\n{\"invoice_number\":null,\"invoice_date\":null,\"supplier_name\":null,\"customer_name\":null,\"subtotal\":null,\"tax\":null,\"total\":null,\"currency\":null,\n\"line_items\":[{\"description\":null,\"quantity\":null,\"unit_price\":null,\"line_total\":null}],\n\"confidence\":{\"invoice_number\":0,\"invoice_date\":0,\"supplier_name\":0,\"customer_name\":0,\"subtotal\":0,\"tax\":0,\"total\":0,\"currency\":0},\n\"notes\":\"\"}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "batching": {}
      },
      "name": "Extract Fields (LLM)",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
      "typeVersion": 1.7,
      "position": [
        1120,
        112
      ],
      "id": "a99b1df9-d921-439e-b5b7-18132c74bbe0"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "model": {
          "__rl": true,
          "value": "gpt-4o-mini",
          "mode": "list",
          "cachedResultName": "gpt-4o-mini"
        },
        "options": {
          "temperature": 0
        }
      },
      "name": "OpenAI Chat Model",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.lmChatOpenAi",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        1120,
        320
      ],
      "id": "d91b8dce-966c-407a-b0d0-42333e2d91b7",
      "credentials": {
        "openAiApi": {
          "id": null,
          "name": "",
          "__aiGatewayManaged": true
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForEachItem",
        "jsCode": "const raw = ($json.text || $json.output || '').toString();\nlet obj;\ntry {\n  const cleaned = raw.replace(/```json|```/g, '').trim();\n  obj = JSON.parse(cleaned.slice(cleaned.indexOf('{'), cleaned.lastIndexOf('}') + 1));\n} catch (e) {\n  return { json: { ok: false, message: 'Model did not return valid JSON' } };\n}\nconst num = v => {\n  if (v === null || v === undefined || v === '') return null;\n  const n = typeof v === 'number' ? v : Number(String(v).replace(/[^0-9.\\-]/g, ''));\n  return Number.isFinite(n) ? n : null;\n};\nconst str = v => (v === null || v === undefined || String(v).trim() === '' ? null : String(v).trim());\nlet date = str(obj.invoice_date);\nif (date && !(/^\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}$/.test(date) && !isNaN(Date.parse(date)))) date = null;\nlet cur = str(obj.currency); cur = cur && /^[A-Za-z]{3}$/.test(cur) ? cur.toUpperCase() : null;\nconst items = Array.isArray(obj.line_items) ? obj.line_items.map(i => ({\n  description: str(i.description), quantity: num(i.quantity), unit_price: num(i.unit_price), line_total: num(i.line_total)\n})).filter(i => i.description || i.line_total !== null) : [];\nreturn { json: { ok: true, invoice: {\n  invoice_number: str(obj.invoice_number), invoice_date: date, supplier_name: str(obj.supplier_name),\n  customer_name: str(obj.customer_name), subtotal: num(obj.subtotal), tax: num(obj.tax), total: num(obj.total),\n  currency: cur, confidence: obj.confidence || {}, raw_json: obj }, line_items: items } };"
      },
